1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Open Marvelous Designer, we can see five main windows

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The one on the left is our library window

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Here you can quickly call long-use files

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Click the Add button to add a long-use folder for easy use

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Double-click to open the clothing file

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,000
After selecting a folder, click the name again to rename the folder

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Quickly double-click the folder name to open the folder

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Double-click to open the virtual model

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
There is a history record window on the side

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Single-click to open it

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Click the Add button to add a history record

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
After selecting a history record, click the name again to rename it

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Quickly double-click the history record to read the history record

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
After reading the history record, go back to the location of the history record and delete the current record

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
At the bottom left is the modular configurator

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Here you can use all kinds of clothing in the library as needed and freely match

17
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Open the folder and select the clothing you need

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
At the bottom window, you can see that the clothing will be divided into several parts

19
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
You can combine according to your needs

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
This is the 3D window, you can simulate clothing and adjust it

21
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
3D window

22
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
On the left side of the 3D window, there is a vertical map menu

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Used to adjust the display settings of the 3D window

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The mouse clicks on the icon, you can see all the options

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
For example, display clothing elements, etc.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
And adjust the display style of the model, etc.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:04,000
In the 2D window next to it, you can edit and adjust the clothing version

28
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The window on the upper right is the object window

29
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Here you can see all the materials for the clothing

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
For example, the button, the back of the eyes, etc.

31
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
When selecting a material in the object window

32
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
There will be corresponding attributes in the property editor at the bottom

33
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
In the property editor

34
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
You can adjust its properties according to your needs

35
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The upper right corner can be switched to the mode

36
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The simulation mode is used to simulate the fashion mode

37
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The animation mode is used to create the fashion animation mode

38
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
After entering the action file, you can simulate and record the fashion animation

39
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
In the module mode, you can edit, adjust and save the fashion module

40
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
To create all kinds of clothing

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
The next mode is UV editor mode

42
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
In the UV editor mode, you can adjust the UV layout of the clothing

43
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The last mode is carving mode

44
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:10,000
In the carving mode, you can use various brushes to carve the clothing

45
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:16,000
For example, use the smooth tool and click and drag the mouse on the clothing

46
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
You can make the fold of the clothing become smooth

47
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Back to the simulation mode

48
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
At this time, the lower right corner can also change the window display button

49
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
You can select all windows or single windows according to your needs

